    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 733,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137325,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 49,
        "headingId": 733,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Seborrhoeic keratoses are benign intraepithelial neoplastic squamous proliferations encountered on ageing skin.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 969,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 734,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137326,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 49,
        "headingId": 734,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8052/0 Seborrhoeic keratosis</p>\r\n<p>8052/0 Irritated seborrhoeic keratosis</p>\r\n<p>8052/0 Stucco keratosis</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 970,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 735,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137327,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 49,
        "headingId": 735,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F21.0 Seborrhoeic keratosis</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 971,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 736,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137328,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 49,
        "headingId": 736,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> senile wart; seborrhoeic wart; basal cell papilloma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 972,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 737,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137329,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 49,
        "headingId": 737,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Irritated seborrhoeic keratosis; stucco keratosis</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 973,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 738,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137330,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 49,
        "headingId": 738,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Seborrhoeic keratoses are found on periocular skin, including the lid margin.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 974,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 739,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137331,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 49,
        "headingId": 739,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients with seborrhoeic keratosis present with a papillomatous, most often sessile tumour with a stuck-on appearance. The papules or plaques are tan to brown and keratotic; owing to the sometimes heavy pigmentation, they can clinically impress as naevi. An acute onset of multiple seborrhoeic keratosis can occur in the setting of internal malignancies, known as the Leser&ndash;Tr&eacute;lat sign {8682971}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 975,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 740,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137332,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 49,
        "headingId": 740,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Seborrhoeic keratosis is most often diagnosed at an older age (&gt;&nbsp;50&nbsp;years). There is no known sex predisposition.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 976,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 741,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137333,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 49,
        "headingId": 741,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Age is a widely acknowledged risk factor for seborrhoeic keratosis. A proposed association with HPV is contested, especially for non-genital lesions {2543229;35066969}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 977,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 742,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137334,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 49,
        "headingId": 742,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Seborrhoeic keratosis is associated with ultraviolet (UV) radiation with a typical UV radiation signature, with the majority of alterations being C&gt;T and CC&gt;TT base changes at dipyrimidinic sites {28410231}. Somatic mutations have been reported in <em>FGFR3</em>, which may result in increased keratinocyte proliferation and reduced apoptosis {15772091;16338952;16778799;20420824}. Other mutated genes include <em>PIK3CA</em>, <em>KRAS</em>, <em>HRAS</em>, <em>EGFR</em>, and <em>AKT1</em> {19845664;23739246;28410231}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 984,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 749,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137335,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 49,
        "headingId": 749,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Seborrhoeic keratosis is a papillomatous, sometimes pigmented tumour with a broad base.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 978,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 743,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137336,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 49,
        "headingId": 743,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>A well-demarcated, thickened epidermal layer due to an increase in basaloid keratinocytes with a flat or reticulated base is seen. Mitoses are rare. The basal epithelial cell layer often contains intracellular pigment. Horn cysts can be found between the basal cells and at the tumour surface hyperkeratosis. There may be lymphoplasmacellular inflammation at the tumour base {33958512}. Different growth patterns and subtypes may be encountered, and they are described in greater detail in the <em>Skin tumours</em> volume of this series [[WHO Classification of Tumours Editorial Board. Skin Tumours. Lyon (France): International Agency for Research on Cancer; 2025. (WHO Classification of Tumours Series, 5th ed.; vol. 12). https://publications.iarc.who.int/650.]].</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 979,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 744,
    "contributions": [
      {
